<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernat Guillem of Cerdanya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1117</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernat Guillem was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> from 1109 to 1117, succeeding his brother William Jordan, who had gone on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> and become count of Tripoli. He was the last of the line of counts of Cerdanya descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfred-the-hairy">Wilfred the Hairy</a>, and on his death without heirs the county passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iii-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer III of Barcelona</a>.</p></div>
